# llm-council-plus — architecture cheat sheet

Hosted essay-writing app. Auth-required. All LLM calls go through OpenRouter.

## Stack

- **Backend**: FastAPI (`uv run uvicorn backend.main:app`), Python 3.10+, `uv` deps.
- **Frontend**: React + Vite. Production build deploys to a static host; reads `VITE_API_URL`.
- **Auth + DB**: Supabase (auth.users + RLS-protected tables).
- **LLM provider**: OpenRouter only (`OPENROUTER_API_KEY` server-side).
- **Hosting**: Backend on Render (`https://writer-1tp5.onrender.com`); GitHub Actions cron pings `/healthz` every 14 min to dodge the 15-min cold-start.

## Backend layout (relative imports only — `from .x import y`)

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `backend/main.py` | FastAPI app, CORS, streaming endpoint, route mounting. |
| `backend/auth.py` | Supabase auth router; exports `get_current_user` dependency + `AuthUser`. |
| `backend/sessions.py` | `/sessions` router — essay flow state (topic, so_what, draft, word_target, council_config). |
| `backend/council_config.py` | `/council-config` router — per-user default council (Supabase `user_council_config`). |
| `backend/council.py` | 3-stage orchestration. `resolve_council_config()` resolves personas+models per call. |
| `backend/prompts.py` | Default persona prompts; `format_word_target_block()`; `PERSONA_KEYS`. |
| `backend/voice_profile.py` | Per-user voice profile (Supabase-backed). Rules / reference paragraphs / inferred style / preferred authors / pending-review queue. |
| `backend/voice_library.py` | Invisible voice scaffolding: random pick from `voice_library`, rendered into Stage 1 + Chairman prompts. |
| `backend/storage.py` | Conversation persistence (file-based, `data/conversations/{id}.json`). |
| `backend/supabase_client.py` | Single `get_supabase()` client. |

## Frontend layout

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `frontend/src/App.jsx` | Top-level shell. Resolves `currentSessionId`, `currentCouncil`, `currentWordTarget`. Wires SSE streaming. |
| `frontend/src/api.js` | API client. Exports `API_BASE`, `warmUpBackend()`, `api.{auth,councilConfig,sessions,memory,voiceProfile,models}`. |
| `frontend/src/contexts/AuthContext.jsx` | In-memory token (no localStorage). `useCallback` on `clearError` is required. |
| `frontend/src/components/Login.jsx` | Login/signup, warm-up status, never-empty error fallback. |
| `frontend/src/components/EssayFlow.jsx` | 3-step input flow with word-target picker + per-essay council override. |
| `frontend/src/components/CouncilConfig.jsx` | The single source-of-truth council picker. Pulls full OpenRouter catalog. |
| `frontend/src/components/CouncilChips.jsx` | Live persona/chairman status during generation. |
| `frontend/src/components/Settings.jsx` | One Council tab (the user-facing one). LLM API Keys tab is hidden. |

## HTTP routes (verified)

```
GET    /                                        root health
GET    /healthz                                  cheap liveness (warm-up + cron)

POST   /auth/signup                              public
POST   /auth/login                               public — returns {access_token, refresh_token, user}
POST   /auth/logout                              authed
GET    /auth/me                                  authed

GET    /council-config                           authed — per-user default
PUT    /council-config                           authed — validate >=2 enabled, all enabled have a model

POST   /sessions                                 authed — body may include word_target
GET    /sessions/memory-check?topic=...          authed — silent past-essay lookup
GET    /sessions/{id}                            authed
PATCH  /sessions/{id}                            authed — accepts word_target, council_config

GET    /api/voice-profile?essay_type=general     authed — full profile incl. pending_suggestions
POST   /api/voice-profile?essay_type=general     authed — body: {rules?, reference_paragraphs?, inferred_style?, preferred_authors?}
POST   /api/voice-profile/suggest-rules          authed — runs LLM extraction; appends to pending_suggestions
POST   /api/voice-profile/accept-suggestion      authed — promotes pending → rules
POST   /api/voice-profile/reject-suggestion      authed — drops a pending entry

POST   /api/intake/questions                     authed — single LLM call: 3-5 probing questions for topic+audience
POST   /api/intake/core-idea                     authed — single LLM call: 1-paragraph brief from topic+audience+Q&A

GET    /api/models                               full live OpenRouter catalog
GET    /api/conversations                        list metadata
POST   /api/conversations                        create
GET    /api/conversations/{id}                   full convo
DELETE /api/conversations/{id}                   delete
POST   /api/conversations/{id}/message/stream    authed — SSE stream of stage1/2/3
GET    /api/settings                             legacy/admin
PUT    /api/settings                             legacy/admin
```

## Runtime config resolution (the truth)

For every streamed message in `/api/conversations/{id}/message/stream`, the backend resolves config in this order:

1. `essay_sessions.council_config` / `.word_target` (per-essay override from EssayFlow Step 4)
2. `user_council_config` row (per-user default — `Settings → Council`)
3. `factory_council_config()` (hardcoded in `council_config.py`)

Same precedence for `word_target`. `data/settings.json` is **not** consulted for council selection in the auth path — only as an index-based fallback for missing model strings inside `resolve_council_config`.

### Voice scaffolding

For every run, the backend also picks one row from `voice_library` (44 example essays) and injects it as `{library_voice_block}` into Stage 1 personas + Chairman as a tonal anchor. Selection is seeded by `session_id` so re-runs of the same essay reuse the same anchor. The chosen `voice_library_id` is pinned on `essay_sessions`. **Users never see library content.**

User voice profile (`voice_profiles` table, per `(user_id, essay_type)`) injects as `{voice_profile_block}` and overrides any stylistic preference of either the council or the library voice.

### Temperatures (creativity-tuned for personal essays)

- Stage 1 personas: **0.95** (council_temperature)
- Voice Guardian persona override: **0.65** (cooler so it doesn't invent rules)
- Stage 2 (peer ranking): **0.3** (must stay deterministic for parsing)
- Stage 3 (Chairman): **0.85** (chairman_temperature)
- `CouncilPersona.temperature` is an optional per-persona override; falls back to council_temperature when None.

## Conventions to preserve

- **Relative imports** in backend (`from .config import ...`). Run via `uv run python -m backend.main`.
- **Model IDs prefixed**: `openrouter:anthropic/claude-sonnet-4`. Strip prefix before calling OpenRouter.
- **Persona keys**: `architect`, `editor`, `devils_advocate`, `voice_guardian` (stable; do not rename).
- **Streaming abort**: inject raw `Request` to use `request.is_disconnected()`. Do not block on it from a Pydantic body.
- **CORS**: `backend/main.py` auto-allows `*.vercel.app`, `*.netlify.app`, `*.onrender.com`, `*.pages.dev`, `*.github.io`. Custom domains via `FRONTEND_ORIGINS` env var.
- **Errors must surface**: in React, never wrap a thrown error in a generic message. Use `extractError()` in `api.js`. Do not add `clearError`-style functions to `useEffect` deps without `useCallback`.
- **Migrations**: SQL in `supabase/migrations/`. Apply manually via Supabase SQL editor; verify with `uv run python -m backend.scripts.verify_council_extensions`.
- **No new commits without explicit user request.**

## Environment variables

Backend (`backend/.env` locally; Render dashboard in prod):
- `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`
- `FRONTEND_ORIGINS` (optional, comma-separated, prod custom domains)

Frontend (`frontend/.env.production` for prod build):
- `VITE_API_URL=https://writer-1tp5.onrender.com`
